WEBVTT

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.130
Sorry! I need a short break.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.240
Those guys from Dotsuku Zone 
just keep coming after us.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.930
On top of getting harder to 
handle, they've taken the

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.580
form of human beings to get close 
to us and take the Prism Stones.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.380
We don't know where they're 
going to come from.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.290
We have to stay focused.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.280
Get out there, defense!

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.990
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.660
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:51.430
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:55.900
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.600
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.740
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.340
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.350
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.150
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:14.950
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.920
<i>we both</i>

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.260
<i>become stronger</i>

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.830
<i>and closer</i>

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.830
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.400
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.570
<i>Don't you know that good fortune</i>

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:33.140
<i>comes to the gates of laughter?
Out with the negative!</i>

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:39.310
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:40.610
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.080
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.120
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.390
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are</i>

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.460
<i>Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:57.200
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.060
Watch the ball!

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.570
What's wrong? You're not moving fast enough!

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:10.840
Wow!

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:11.980
Fuji-P!

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.480
Look at all his fans!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.850
Excuse me!

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.190
Wait a minute!

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.790
What? Don't come in here.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.420
What...?

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.030
You're kidding!

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.320
He got past Fuji-P?

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.720
But don't you think he's good-looking?

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.890
I'm sorry for interrupting your practice.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.360
Who are you?

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.320
I just transferred to this school today.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.450
I'm a first-year student. 
My name is Kiriya Irisawa.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:18.070
"BEWARE! THE YOUNG TRANSFER STUDENT"

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.740
"BEWARE! THE YOUNG TRANSFER STUDENT"

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.040
Science Room

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.460
Everybody! I have big news!

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:36.070
A transfer student beat Fuji-P in soccer.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.810
Are you serious?

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.260
He beat Fujimura-kun?

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:43.230
He just transferred to the school today.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.010
Let's all go watch.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.260
What about you, Yukishiro-san?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.300
Wait a minute!

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.350
We don't have much time before 
the Science Project Presentation.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.220
You can't be goofing off now.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.720
And asking Honoka to go along is outrageous.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.490
Why are you so wound up?

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.390
Don't be like that.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.240
What's wrong?

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.800
You don't understand, do you?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.980
This year is our best chance of taking first 
place at the Science Project Presentation.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:12.860
After all, this year...

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.290
We're going to be presenting 
Honoka's science project,

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.140
so we're guaranteed to take the Grand Prix.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.190
He had a perfect score 
on the admissions exam.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.350
Are you serious?

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:34.100
He's smart!

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.150
On top of that, he's so cute!

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.220
Kiriya Irisawa, huh?

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:42.230
For a first-year student, he might 
just be another ace along with Fuji-P.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.610
Kiriya-kun is the best!

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.440
I wonder if he'll make me his girlfriend.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.740
But he's younger than we are.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.220
What are you saying?

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.040
These days, younger men with a promising 
future are the best catch for a boyfriend.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.730
Kiriya-kun!

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.890
A boyfriend...?

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.120
I would rather have...

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.920
What am I thinking?

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.300
Nagisa!

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.440
Are you okay?

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:17.930
I have no idea what you're thinking.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.440
I'm finished!

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.740
Something's missing.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.090
You have a bottomless pit, don't you?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.530
I wonder if I have some chocolate...

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.120
Do you have time to be eating?

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.350
Wasn't it your turn to answer 
in our math class next period?

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.150
I forgot to prepare for it.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.010
Is that anything new?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.960
You might as well forget 
about it again today,

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.530
and let him scold you.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.000
It doesn't bother me...

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.360
I have a strong ally on my side.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.340
Honoka...!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.620
There she is.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.150
Honoka! I have a favor to ask...

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:22.560
What is that?

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.130
What is this anyway?

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.790
It's a device that generates 
static electricity.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:34.120
I'm using it as a device to create thunder.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.270
Thunder?

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.840
It's a simulation to recreate 
the circulation of air and

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.100
water, using thunder as a hint.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:47.180
In other words, it's like 
creating a miniature earth.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:51.840
I'm going to use that device 
to present an experiment at

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.900
the next Science Project Presentation.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.760
We're going to take the Grand Prix.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.030
By the way, aren't you 
going to eat your lunch?

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:03.860
I don't have time.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.410
If you want, you can eat it.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.510
Really?

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:07.460
Wait a minute!

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:09.610
You can eat mine, too.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.580
Thank you!

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.310
You couldn't eat two, could you?

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:16.210
I'm finished.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.520
You ate it.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.420
I eat in moderation.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:24.360
Is it that late already?

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:26.320
That's right... Next is our math...

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.340
I don't believe I had to 
have supplementary lessons

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.170
until this late just because 
I forgot to prepare for class.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.710
No way!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.660
Are you okay?

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.610
I'm okay... Thanks.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:58.420
You're welcome, Misumi-san...

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.730
How do you know my name?

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.450
Of course I know your name.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:05.000
After all, you're still 
a second-year student,

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.800
but you're already known as 
an ace on the lacrosse team.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:10.300
I'm not that good.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:13.610
Your body is very precious, 
so please be careful.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:14.890
Later.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.310
He's a nice kid.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:27.520
It's almost finished isn't it?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.500
What are we going to name 
this experimental device?

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:33.230
We'll call it Honoka One, of course.

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:34.630
It has to be.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.880
We're guaranteed to take the 
Grand Prix with Honoka One.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:52.820
Excuse me...

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:57.720
Did you want something?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.640
I'm sorry... I couldn't help myself...

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:05.720
By any chance, are you from the 
Girls Division's science club...?

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.690
Yes... I'm Honoka Yukishiro.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.490
Who are you?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:14.100
I'm a first-year student 
in the Boys Division...

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.970
My name is Kiriya Irisawa.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.270
And...?

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.560
Did you want something?

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.840
Honoka! Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.850
Is it really all right for 
me to come to your house?

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.260
Why? Sure it's okay.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:37.960
Let's check the manuscript together.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.260
The transfer student everyone 
has been talking about...

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:44.830
The train is leaving, Yuriko.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.320
If you'll excuse us, We have things to do...

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.800
Since he's here, let me talk to him.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.830
How unusual.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.620
It's the first time I've seen 
you treated like that, Kiriya...

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.560
Idiot! I was just kidding.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:17.620
You just don't understand, do you, Poisonny?

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:21.100
I'm curious about those two.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:25.370
After all, it's a fact that they 
defeated both Pisard and Gekidrago.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:28.840
It wouldn't be any fun if I got 
rid of them too easily, would it?

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.540
You're good at making excuses, aren't you?

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.650
What about you?

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:39.670
Shouldn't you be thinking of 
a way to restore your honor?

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.360
You don't have to tell me that.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.940
I know!

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:45.520
I'm glad.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.990
Good luck, Poisonny.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:53.800
Thank you, my adorable 
little brother, Kiriya.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:55.960
By the way...

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.400
You're really drawing a lot 
of attention in that get-up.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.110
You're kidding!

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:07.510
I don't believe this.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:13.540
I'm so glad I joined the science club...

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.360
Otherwise, I would never 
have met you, Honoka.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.190
Yuriko...

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:21.490
Let's take the Grand Prix 
with Honoka One, okay?

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.190
Let's do our best.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.280
According to Yuriko, they're 
out to win the Grand Prix.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:50.310
I guess Yukishiro-san's 
role is big, isn't it?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.900
Yuriko has always worked so hard.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:55.560
I hope they take the Grand Prix.

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:58.970
Honoka... Don't be nervous.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:02.480
Don't worry... I'll be right 
there to give you my support.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:03.370
Yuriko...?

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:06.720
You're buttoned up all wrong.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:11.370
Nagisa! Where's Mipple? Where is she mepo?

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:12.630
Mipple... Mipple...

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.680
Stop with all that "Mipple" already.
You're getting on my nerves.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.860
We didn't come to see Mipple today...

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.520
We came to root for Honoka.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.040
Honoka's got a good head on her shoulders...

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:24.920
She doesn't need you to succeed...

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.900
Just shut up!

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:28.260
Misumi-san.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:32.490
You're here, too.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.050
Are you alone, Kiriya-kun?

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.000
No... I'm with the team captain...

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.300
Captain...?

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.710
Fuji-P...

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:45.340
Hello, Misumi-san.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.410
What are you doing here?

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:49.710
I came to give Honoka my support.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:53.690
Thank you.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:59.820
Captain... I just remembered 
something urgent I have to do.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.690
I'm sorry... I'd better go.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:11.820
I'd better...

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:13.970
Misumi-san.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:15.980
Yes?

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.250
I don't believe this.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.690
Honoka's the third entry.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.740
What am I going to do?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:30.820
I should say something.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.140
What do we have in common?

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.710
Calm down.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.300
That's it! It's Honoka.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:38.140
Honoka's his childhood friend, 
and she's my friend, too.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:40.070
That's the perfect thing to have in common...

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.300
So what should I say first?

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:46.520
It would be nice if Honoka's experiment 
is a success, wouldn't it?

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.160
That's good... it sounds so natural.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.270
Here we go...!

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.710
My heart is...!

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:56.810
Stop that!

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.720
Honoka's experiment...

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:08.430
We would like to start the 
15th Annual Southwest Area

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:11.980
Middle Schools Science Project Presentation.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:19.070
After the eight experiments 
have been presented,

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:25.700
the judges will judge each entry, 
and we will be announcing the

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:30.170
two winning entries, and the 
winning Grand Prix entry.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:34.120
Are you ready? Let's take the 
Grand Prix with Honoka One.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:44.800
That was a very good presentation...

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:49.860
Next, we have Verone Academy's 
Girls Division's presentation

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:53.070
of their research using thunder as a hint.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:15:03.800
Our research began with finding 
the reason why thunder occurs.

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:09.110
A cloud formed by a strong 
rising current of air

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.220
produced by terrestrial heat, 
grows bigger and bigger...

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:16.260
Thus, increasing the amount 
of plus and minus electricity

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.230
within the cloud, and the 
large amount of electricity

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:23.240
passes through the air between 
the cloud and the ground.

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.700
This is what produces thunder.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:28.900
The rain from this cloud returns 
to the rivers and ponds,

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.680
turning once again into rising 
currents of air, and forming a cloud.

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:37.980
We wanted to build a miniature 
earth using this as a basis.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:41.910
This miniature simulation 
device, which will recreate

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:46.290
thunder, clouds, and water, 
is our presentation today.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.400
What is that?

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.680
Due to the inability of our 
power supply room to control

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:07.480
the power, the voltage of our 
equipment has become unstable.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.890
The exit is this way, everyone.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:11.620
Please calmly evacuate the room.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.760
Just what you'd expect from Fuji-P.

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.220
I don't have time to be impressed, do I?

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:18.980
Hurry, Honoka!

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:19.860
You, too, Yuriko.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.370
Let's run away, Yuriko.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:24.730
But the Honoka One...

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.420
Hurry, Yuriko!

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.790
Just get outside.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.440
Don't tell me this is...?

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.910
Go down the stairs, and go outside.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:46.320
Misumi-san! Honoka!

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.260
Someone! Open the door!

00:16:58.680 --> 00:16:59.600
I thought so!

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.570
It can't be! What is this?

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:17.350
Nagisa!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:18.760
Honoka!

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:27.760
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:48.550
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.420
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:55.290
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:57.790
What's happening?

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:01.190
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:04.630
Go back to where you came from!

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:18.970
I never expected it to turn into Zakenna!

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:20.310
We have to do something.

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:22.480
What is this?

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:25.240
Is this Honoka One?

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:30.840
Don't! Don't destroy it.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:34.290
We made this for everyone's 
sake... for Honoka's sake...

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:38.700
We worked really hard to make this 
so we could win the Grand Prix!

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.170
So, please! Don't destroy it.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:43.670
Zakenna!

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:44.970
It's dangerous! Get out of the way!

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:50.100
Are you okay?

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.160
Don't...

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.120
How could you...!

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:57.480
I won't forgive you!

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:59.450
You're watching from somewhere, aren't you?

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.720
Come out here!

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:05.470
That's incentive enough to come out.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:11.930
Why you...!

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:14.240
I'm so scared!

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:18.100
You're making me mad!

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:26.030
We have to do something.

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.480
I feel bad for Yuriko and you, but...

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:30.300
Is it okay?

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:31.120
It's okay.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:32.480
I understand.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.960
Go ahead, and put an end to them now!

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:40.980
Ready, White?

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:45.200
Misumi-san...

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:47.500
Black Thunder!

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.770
White Thunder!

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:57.980
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:00.780
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:05.250
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:30.940
What happened to Honoka One?

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:33.860
That's strange...

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:36.510
I'm sure it had turned into 
some kind of a monster...

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:39.150
Don't you remember, Yuriko?

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:43.190
You got caught in the accident with the 
power supply room, and you lost consciousness.

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:44.850
Is that what happened?

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:45.770
That's right.

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:46.490
That's very good.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.400
Be quiet!

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:52.700
Thank you all for your patience...

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:55.630
The power supply has been restored,

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:59.000
so we will continue our science 
experiment presentations.

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:04.150
And that was the result of our research.

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:12.380
We worked very hard on this device for 
the sake of this research presentation.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:16.900
This device is the fruit of the efforts 
of all the members of our science club.

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:19.620
I think everyone worked very hard for this.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.730
But if it weren't for one person,

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:25.460
I don't think we would have gotten this far.

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:30.760
So we decided to name this 
device after that person.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:37.220
Hono...

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:40.510
It's Yuriko One.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:44.010
That's what we all decided.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:46.500
Yuriko really worked hard, didn't she?

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:50.460
Without you, Yuriko... We wouldn't be here.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:54.220
Everyone...

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:58.160
That's the end of our research presentation.

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:25.320
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:26.860
<i>Get you!</i>

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:29.560
<i>L-O-V-E Love Love, get you!</i>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.300
<i>I can't do this!</i>

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:35.570
<i>I'd rather be a young lady than a fighter and</i>

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:38.000
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:22:38.100 --> 00:22:42.140
<i>And melt your body and soul into sweets</i>

00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:47.850
<i>like chocolate parfait or handsome men</i>

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:51.580
<i>I'm at the age to seriously 
fall head over heels in love</i>

00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:55.320
<i>I wanted to confess my love again today</i>

00:22:56.450 --> 00:22:59.690
<i>For the sake of the earth 
For the sake of everyone</i>

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:06.330
<i>That's good, too, but haven't 
you forgotten something?</i>

00:23:07.430 --> 00:23:10.700
<i>I'm a teenager with a</i>

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:13.940
<i>heart throbbing exciting dream</i>

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:16.670
<i>I don't want to lose that</i>

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:20.450
<i>normal everyday routine</i>

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:22.950
<i>I just can't do this!</i>

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:26.420
<i>It's romance rather than stress, isn't it?</i>

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:28.590
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:31.890
<i>Isn't that the best source of power?</i>

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:34.930
<i>I just can't do this!</i>

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:38.200
<i>I'd rather cuddle than fight and...</i>

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:40.430
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:42.970
<i>That's the most peaceful way</i>

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:44.370
<i>So why am I</i>

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:45.970
<i>stuffing my face</i>

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:49.670
<i>with chocolates like this?</i>

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:55.360
There's one more of me.

00:23:55.360 --> 00:23:56.700
There's another one of me, too.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:57.890
That couldn't be...!

00:23:57.890 --> 00:23:59.230
They must be impostors.

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:00.270
What's going on?

00:24:00.270 --> 00:24:03.820
I have no idea what's going on, but 
trying to copy us is dangerous.

00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:06.930
That's true... Those guys 
will come after them.

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:08.570
We have to save them!

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:12.630
"ARE YOU KIDDING? PRETTY 
CURE IMPOSTERS GO WILD"

00:24:12.630 --> 00:24:14.480
How will you tell the difference if an

00:24:14.480 --> 00:24:16.500
imposter who looks exactly 
like me appears, Honoka?

00:24:16.500 --> 00:24:18.310
The real one would be fighting with Mepple...

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:18.940
I guess.

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:19.870
What?
